# Local secrets for development. Copy to .env.development (git-ignored, read from the main checkout by
# every worktree) and fill in. Never commit real values. Every key and what it does: docs/reference/secrets.md.

# Clerk *development* instance secret key (Clerk dashboard > Development > API keys). Only sk_test_ keys are
# accepted. `npm run dev` in a worktree uses it (apps/desktop/tools/dev-account.mjs) to sign the sandbox into
# its own test account, and `npm run dev -- --prune` to delete that account again.
CODYNC_CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me

# The device certificate key (Ed25519 private key as JWK JSON) of the development cloud: `wrangler secret put
# DEVICE_CERT_KEY --env dev` from cloud/ (cloud/README.md). Dev hosts compile in its public half.
# CODYNC_DEVICE_CERT_KEY={"kty":"OKP","crv":"Ed25519","d":"…","x":"…"}

# The Codync Cloud sealing keys of the development cloud (`wrangler secret put CLOUD_SECRET_KEYS --env dev` from
# cloud/; cloud/README.md): the only copy, since a Worker secret can't be read back; losing it locks every saved
# provider key and every cloud computer's keeper vault. Never production's.
# CODYNC_CLOUD_SECRET_KEYS=k1:…
